      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that the world is just code speaks to a deep, existential weariness, a kind of burnout from constant digital input. It's understandable that when the external world feels abstract, your own sense of self begins to feel like a corrupted file. If you feel like you are just noise, perhaps finding a way to intentionally disconnect from the screen and engage with something purely physical, like a real texture or sound, might help anchor you back to something tangible.",
      "source": "target",
